# Data (never committed; see README for how to fetch).
#
# Written as `data/*` rather than `data/` deliberately. Git will not descend
# into an excluded directory, so a plain `data/` makes every negation below
# silently dead: "it is not possible to re-include a file if a parent directory
# of that file is excluded." `data/*` excludes the contents while leaving the
# directory itself traversable, which is what lets the tag cache through.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep

# The Last.fm tag cache IS committed. It represents tens of thousands of
# rate-limited requests at ~4 req/s, so a fresh clone that silently refetched it
# would cost hours.
!data/tags/

# Model artifacts and caches
*.pt
*.pth
*.npy
*.npz
artifacts/
.cache/

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Node (Phase 6)
node_modules/
.next/

# Local tooling config, not project code
.claude/

# Working notes kept out of history on purpose. The reasoning that matters is
# preserved in the commit messages.
COORDINATION.md
REVIEW-*.md
CLAUDE.md

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
